About
I am a final-year BS Bioinformatics student at Government College University Faisalabad, Pakistan, passionate about using computational tools and machine learning to solve real biological problems. My work sits at the intersection of biology, data science, and artificial intelligence — from classifying diseases using ML models to predicting drug-target interactions in silico. I have collaborated on international research with Gachon University, South Korea, completed ML internships, and developed bioinformatics pipelines for DNA sequence analysis and computational drug discovery. I am currently training in AI and Deep Learning under Pakistan's national NAVTTC program. My goal is to contribute to the field of biomedical data science through research, open-source tools, and continuous learning.
